	IPR1-HY-NOB: Hello Brian
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You require answers. I know all. I shall bestow them upon you. But first, there is work to be done
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Digest the statements. And once you are ready, I shall answer what you wish.
=> END

~ eye1
if fear.fear < 89 && fear.fear > 50
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You did not read enought
	Brian: What?? How many more.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Pacience. I will answer everything soon
elif fear.fear > 89:
	do stop_timer()
	{Since this dialog is quite long, I added a chance to skip it}
	{However, if you haven't seen it yet, I recomend reading though it}
	{Otherwise you'll be really confused}
	- Skip
		Skip everyting, or just the first part
		- everything
			do SignalManager.change_room.emit()
		- just the first part
			=> ending
	- Don't
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You are ready. Ask what you wish!
	Brian: I wish to know, why did the house target me, Margaret, Alice and Dan. What did we to deserve such fate?
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You were scared
	Brian: What?
	IPR1-HY-NOB: The house feeds on fear of disorientation. You were scared to go in. But drawn to you're fate.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: If you weren't scare, It would have not bothered.
	Brian: And why then did it let ME leave while EVERYONE else died??
	IPR1-HY-NOB: To feed on you
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Look at yourself. You still fear it, you still feed it.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: All the others would have slowly moved on
	IPR1-HY-NOB: But instead, you are drawn deeper, by the guilt
	IPR1-HY-NOB: It may claime you eventually. But it will savour your paranoia for long time, before that happens
	Brian: [Heavy breathing]
	Brian: Ok... ok... fine... Then, how I do save them. How to save them from that house!
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You can't.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: There is no way to save someone in the house
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You cannot save them
	Brian: What... no..
	IPR1-HY-NOB: There is not even enought of them left to save
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Take Alice. Do you know what she is in right now.
	Brian: No, please, I don't want to know.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Oh.. but you do... I can sence your curiosity.. and fear
	IPR1-HY-NOB: She no longer feels the stare of mirror's gaze
	IPR1-HY-NOB: No, instead she is the mirror
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Twisted and bend like a funhouse show, endlessly shattered and contorted.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And she is mad. Mad but scared. And in so much pain
	IPR1-HY-NOB: She cannot remember how she got here. But she remembers you
	IPR1-HY-NOB: The twisted figure that pretended to be her friend
	IPR1-HY-NOB: That brought her to her doom
	IPR1-HY-NOB: That lied that it will rescue her
	Brian: [Sobing] I beg you, no more
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Or, how about Margaret.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: She still sits on those stairs
	IPR1-HY-NOB: She was one to go quickly
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Despite the twisting, she still feels the hight she is in
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And she refuses to look down.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Even thogh, it might be up
	IPR1-HY-NOB: She goes down and down the stair
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Sometimes, she feels like she is standing in place, and the stares walk her
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And sometimes, she remembers a shadow. A heinous reminder of why she is here. You.
	Brian: [In tears] Please. I did not ask for this
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Oh, but you did
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You cannot lie to me Brian
	IPR1-HY-NOB: I know. And you know, I won't lie to you
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Not like you, to poor Dan
	IPR1-HY-NOB: "We go together"
	IPR1-HY-NOB: He is still there
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Still searching for you
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Still partially sane
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Sometimes, he thinks you went ahead and he fell behind
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Sometimes, he thinks you found a door, but it lock behind you
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And sometimes, he thinks the hallway ate you
	IPR1-HY-NOB: But he remembers the promise
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And so he keeps searching, calling, for one who he will never see
	Brian: [On the verge of breakdow] Fine, you monster
	Brian: If I cannot save them, how do I avenge them
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Oh.. you can't.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: The house will exist as long as it is feared.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And it has plenty of victims thanks to you
	IPR1-HY-NOB: It can strech their misoury for centuries.
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And even if, as long as you live, it can always feast on you
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And those unfortunate enought to open a door ment for you
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You cannot avange them
	IPR1-HY-NOB: And you will help perpetuate the thing, that killed them
	Brian: [Broken] Fine. Fine
	Brian: If thats how it is, how do I save myself
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You can't...
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You are marked by the house
	IPR1-HY-NOB: It's only a matter of time, before it swallows you to
	IPR1-HY-NOB: But don't get your hopes up
	IPR1-HY-NOB: The guilt will not leave you
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Only grow worst
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You will never find peace
	Brian: [Broken] Why?? Why can't you offer any hope or help
	Brian: What did I do to you to torment me so
	IPR1-HY-NOB: I am only doing what you wanted
	IPR1-HY-NOB: you wanted to know the truth
	IPR1-HY-NOB: I tell only truth
	Brian: I.. no... there must be.. something...
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You know I am truthfull. And you know there is no hope
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Goodbye Brian
	IPR1-HY-NOB: Feel free to come agin, if any more questions arise
	=> ending
else:
	IPR1-HY-NOB: You did not read enought
=> END

